From: Dan Yocom <630234+danyocom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:12:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/14] Support the in-game reset in Golden Sun: Dark Dawn

The game replaces the SDK interrupt dispatcher with one that picks the pending
interrupt with a single clz instead of a loop, makes its whole body conditional,
and calls the handler with blx. None of the stock dispatcher's instructions
survive, so it needs a dispatch part of its own.

Two differences shape that part. The dispatcher keeps the end of the handler
table in lr, so no copy of the table address is needed, and it has not
acknowledged the interrupt at the point the jump takes over, so the write to
REG_IF moves into the patch. When nothing is pending the replaced code called
the BIOS return, which never comes back, so the patch branches to it instead.

The pattern covers the dispatcher from its first instruction to its call, with
only the literal pool offset left free, which is a tighter match than the stock
dispatcher's four instructions. Since this dispatcher has no literal holding the
address it runs from, the relocation check is that autoload places it in ITCM.
